# Local data — never commit. This is the whole point of the project.
# Leading slash matters: a bare `data/` also swallows research/tise_research/data/.
/data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.db-journal
*.csv
!service/tests/**/*.csv
!ml/**/fixtures/*.csv

# Local-only working notes — never published
CLAUDE.local.md
*.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json

# Screenshots. **No screenshot is published, without exception** (Akash, 2026-09-03).
#
# The previous scheme ignored the directory and re-admitted eleven "safe" T5 spike files
# one pattern at a time. Two of them showed a live Booking.com hotel search, one with a
# full tracking URL in the address bar — in the repository whose headline claim is that no
# full URL is ever stored. They were judged safe once, by someone looking at them, and the
# judgement did not survive being looked at again. A rule that needs a person to classify
# each image correctly fails on the image nobody looked at twice, so there is no
# allow-list any more.
#
# The folder has also been moved out of the repository to `../Tise-evidence/`: a file that
# is not in the working tree cannot be committed by a mistake in this file (D118).
#
# **This deliberately does not ignore `*.png`.** Tise's own icons are product assets and
# must ship. A blanket rule with an exception for them is the same allow-list shape that
# failed above, one typo away from an extension with no icon. Screenshots are excluded by
# *where they are*, and `test_repository.py` fails on any tracked image outside
# `extension/icons/` — a guard that says so out loud rather than one that silently drops
# a file.
Screenshots/
**/Screenshots/

# Belt and braces, path-independent: an export is a profile of a person wherever it lands.
# The `/data/` rule above is anchored on purpose — a bare `data/` would swallow the source
# package `research/tise_research/data/` — and an anchored rule protects one directory, not
# the file. D97: running `analysis/history_shape.py` from `research/` made it write a fresh
# copy of the live Chrome history to `research/data/`, which no rule here covered. It was
# never committed, but nothing except noticing stood in the way.
#
# A history copy is a person's browsing wherever it lands, so these are path-independent and
# named after the *file*, not the directory it happens to be in.
**/tise-export-*.json
**/*.copy
**/*.copy-wal
**/*.copy-shm
**/history-shape-domains-*.md
**/unknown-domains.md
**/ss_tt*.png
**/ss_ta*.png

